        "tool": "colony.push",
        "arguments": {
          "namespace": "bench",
          "question": "How are namespace permissions checked?",
          "content": "Namespace access is granted in a signed, unexpired keyfile Grant. The server verifies the bearer keyfile against the trusted Ed25519 issuer public key on each request, then checks the grant scopes: push requires a matching namespace scope with push=true; ask/pull requires a scope with pull=true. If ask specifies a namespace it must be among those pull-enabled namespaces; otherwise retrieval is limited to all pull-enabled namespaces. Denied checks return HTTP 403. Sources: src/colony/server.py and src/colony/security.py.",
          "sources": [
            {
